% role_policy — define what each human lane may do

# Module: role-policy

Create pure TypeScript policy helpers for roles PM, ENG, DESIGN, QA, observer and
powers run, steer, halt, edit_intent, vote, open_pr. Defaults:
PM all true priority 80; ENG all true priority 70; QA cannot edit intent priority
60; DESIGN cannot halt/open PR priority 50; observer can only steer priority 10.
Unknown roles fail closed as observer. Partial overrides merge per power; unknown
override keys are ignored. `voters` returns unique sorted IDs. Unknown powers
throw. Do not mutate input or perform I/O.
